  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scope",
      "items": [
        "Process contract: issue 2802. Host pipeline: LP-1 to LP-5 (issues 2978-2982) of issue 2977.",
        "Destinations are chosen by SERVER2_LOG_SINKS; local alone skips the collector.",
        "Not deployment evidence; no AWS resource is created by these files."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Incident semantics",
      "items": [
        "Accepted, durable, failed, cancelled and unknown are distinct outcomes.",
        "No URL, body, credential, coordinate, registration ID or notification text enters the event API.",
        "The operator starts from terminal failures and follows parent / shared-owner IDs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Output failure",
      "items": [
        "A blocked stderr sink can lose diagnostics; independent counters expose the gap.",
        "A loss summary is best-effort when output becomes available; logs are not a durable business ledger."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Host pipeline",
      "items": [
        "A start check reads only SERVER2_LOG_* and bucket/region; local alone skips the collector, invalid settings fail it.",
        "The server does not require the collector; a shutdown stops the server first, then the collector drains until delivery is confirmed (at most 75 s).",
        "Each remote destination has its own journal reader, level filter and checkpoint.",
        "Only schema-1 server records at or above the level, and collector records, leave the host.",
        "Loss is visible per destination: status records, overrun records and loopback counters (LP-2).",
        "Boot configuration alone starts shipping; names carry the instance ID (IMDSv2) and boot ID, and an earlier boot on a surviving disk is shipped by its own reader (LP-3).",
        "A Spot notice is recorded, then the server and the collector stop in order within 80 s; without a notice a record is lost only if younger than 60 s (S3) or 10 s (CloudWatch) (LP-4)."
      ]
    }
